welcome back to biomedical data science  and python let's start this lesson and  speak a little bit about data wrangling  how to load transform and start  exploring data  before we start let's discuss data  structures in python there are two  packages that are required to deal with  data that we load numpy and pandas numpy  is the fundamental library of python it  is used to perform scientific computing  it provides high performance  multi-dimensional arrays and tools to  deal with them a numpy array is a grid  of values of the same type let's say  numeric that are indexed by a tuple of  positive integers numpy arrays are fast  easy to understand and give users the  right to perform calculations across  arrays  pandas provides easy to use data  structures and data analysis tools for  manipulating numeric data organized as  data frames  the pandas data frame is a structure  that contains two-dimensional data and  its corresponding labels  data frames are very similar to sql  tables or the spreadsheets that you work  with in excel  in many cases data frames are faster  easier to use and more powerful than  tables or spreadsheets  as you can see in the first data set  that we will explore  the data contains four columns called id  flower tree and bird for each column  there are a number of specimens that are  rows in the table  each row and column have corresponding  cell values  to load the data set into the browser  console download the file to your  computer and then drag and drop it in  the area under the console where it says  drop a file
 

